   padding — so a split code block reads as the same deck. Highlighting (hljs spans) is
   carried verbatim. A single block gets the full width; a very wide line wraps as a last
   resort so it fits without dropping the type below readable. */
section.compare-code-block pre {
  margin: 0; max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md); overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--spectrum-structure) bottom / 100% 3px no-repeat, var(--code-bg);
  padding: var(--sp-md) var(--sp-lg);
  padding-bottom: calc(var(--sp-md) + 0.234375cqi);
