/* ── FONT SCALE ──
 * Global "bump every font up" knob. Each step raises --fs-scale, which
 * the 12 typography tokens multiply into (base.tokens.css). EVERYTHING
 * sized through the tokens grows in lockstep — body, headings, hero,
 * chrome, the three documented between-token raw-cqi sites — so the
 * carefully-tuned proportions hold; only the overall magnitude moves.
 * The normalized footprint targets desk-distance reading; these steps
 * opt UP for projection, large rooms, or accessibility.
 *
 * Scope is native Marp class scoping — no separate mechanism:
 *   one slide  → `<!-- _class: scale-xl -->`   (spot directive)
 *   whole deck → `<!-- class: scale-xl -->`     (global front-matter directive)
 * Composes with any layout/variant (dark, cards-grid, …) since it only
 * sets a custom property. See engineering/typography.md §7 and
 * lib/base/base.docs.md. */
section.scale-l   { --fs-scale: 1.15; }
section.scale-xl  { --fs-scale: 1.3;  }
section.scale-2xl { --fs-scale: 1.5;  }


/* ── BELOW-NOTE fallback ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * CLI wraps trailing <p> in .below-note. In Marp preview the raw <p> needs
 * the same hairline-rule treatment for layouts that use it.
 *
 * NOTE: Marpit's CSS scoper rewrites leading `:is(section.X, ...)` to
 * `div#:$p > svg > foreignobject > section :is(...)` — i.e. it treats
 * the `:is(...)` as a descendant of the slide root rather than the slide
 * itself. So leading sections must be enumerated as a comma-separated
 * union (each gets prefixed individually), not collapsed into `:is()`.
 *                                                                            */
section.cards-grid:not(:has(.below-note)) > :is(ul, ol, blockquote, table) + p,
section.compare-prose:not(:has(.below-note)) > :is(ul, ol, blockquote, table) + p,
section.verdict-grid:not(:has(.below-note)) > :is(ul, ol, blockquote, table) + p,
section.list-criteria:not(:has(.below-note)) > :is(ul, ol, blockquote, table) + p,
