/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * RADAR (radar-beta)
 * ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Mermaid's radar ships its curves gray with no per-curve theme hook, so we
 * paint them from the engine `--cN` categorical palette — like the band cycle
 * — giving each series a distinct, theme-flavoured colour, extensible to eight
 * curves (not the two brand accents this used to hard-code). `--cN-dark` is the
 * saturated stroke tone that flips per canvas (vivid on light, pale on dark).
 * Moved here from radar.styles.css (the NATIVE radar component): this is
 * Mermaid output and belongs with the diagram overrides. `!important` beats
 * Mermaid's auto-emitted inline CSS. (`.radarTitle` is suppressed above.)
 * LOAD-BEARING — render-verified 2026-06-18: stripping ANY radar `!important`
 * group regresses the override (curve fills AE≈230k, axis/graticule AE≈270k vs
 * baseline). These are NOT a removal target; Mermaid's inline styles only yield
 * to `!important`. See engineering/decisions/2026-06-18-chart-mermaid-style-separation.md.
 */
:is(section, figure) .radarGraticule {
  /* Decorative background grid, NOT a category — stays a flat tint (a texture
     pattern here reads as speckle behind the plot). Universal texture channel
     deliberately skipped. See 2026-07-16-universal-texture-channel.md. */
  fill: var(--cat-1-fill) !important;
  fill-opacity: 0.25 !important;
  stroke: var(--diagram-stroke) !important;
  stroke-opacity: 0.20 !important;
  stroke-width: 1 !important;
}
:is(section, figure) .radarAxisLine {
  stroke: var(--diagram-stroke) !important;
  stroke-width: 1.5 !important;
  stroke-opacity: 0.5 !important;
}
