/* ── TIMELINE EVENT WRAPPER ──
 * Mermaid wraps every timeline event in <g class="eventWrapper"> and pins
 * `filter: brightness(120%)` on the class. Their intent is to lighten the
 * event tile so it reads as "inside" the period header above it, but the
 * band cycle already sits at L≈83 — pushing it +20% lightness clamps the
 * G/B channels to 255 and collapses every band into a near-cyan wash
 * (band-1 #BCD5EC → ~#E1FEFE, band-2 #C1E4D5 → ~#E7FEFE — indistinguishable
 * from band-1). Drop the filter so event tiles match their section's band
 * exactly. The size difference (event tile is narrower than the period
 * header above it) is enough to keep the visual hierarchy.
 */
:is(section, figure) .eventWrapper { filter: none !important; }

/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * RELOCATED FROM OWNED COMPONENT FILES (owned chart stylesheets carry zero
 * Mermaid selectors — all third-party CSS lives here). See
 * engineering/decisions/2026-06-18-chart-mermaid-style-separation.md.
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

